### TITLE ###
DefaultRunsWhenNoCommandNamed
### DESCRIPTION ###
The point of the feature: the primary action is reachable without naming it.
### INPUT ###
command add:
    *tokens str
    default
    calls fn():
        print("add {tokens}")

command list:
    calls fn():
        print("list")
### ARGS ###
15m
standup
### STDOUT ###
add [ "15m", "standup" ]

### TITLE ###
NamedSiblingWinsOverDefault
### INPUT ###
command add:
    *tokens str
    default
    calls fn():
        print("add {tokens}")

command list:
    calls fn():
        print("list")
### ARGS ###
list
### STDOUT ###
list

### TITLE ###
DefaultStillInvokableByName
### DESCRIPTION ###
The default keeps its own name, which is what makes it usable as an escape
hatch when a value would otherwise be read as a sibling command.
### INPUT ###
command add:
    *tokens str
    default
    calls fn():
        print("add {tokens}")

command list:
    calls fn():
        print("list")
### ARGS ###
add
list
### STDOUT ###
add [ "list" ]

### TITLE ###
DashDashEscapesSiblingCollision
### DESCRIPTION ###
The conventional escape. `--` suppresses command lookup without suppressing
the routing, so the colliding value reaches the default as data.
### INPUT ###
command add:
    *tokens str
    default
    calls fn():
        print("add {tokens}")

command list:
    calls fn():
        print("list")
### RAW_ARGS ###
--color=never
--
list
### STDOUT ###
add [ "list" ]

### TITLE ###
SharedFlagBeforeDefaultValues
### DESCRIPTION ###
A shared arg is registered on the commands, not the root, so it reaches the
root as an unrecognized flag and has to route along with everything after it.
### INPUT ###
args:
    repeat r str?

command add:
    *tokens str
    default
    calls fn():
        print("add {tokens} repeat={repeat}")

command list:
    calls fn():
        print("list")
### ARGS ###
--repeat
1d
8:45
standup
### STDOUT ###
add [ "8:45", "standup" ] repeat=1d

### TITLE ###
DefaultInsideNamespace
### DESCRIPTION ###
The rule is the same at every level, so a bare namespace runs its own default
rather than erroring.
### INPUT ###
command remote:
    timeout int = 30

    command add:
        name str
        default
        calls fn():
            print("add {name} timeout={timeout}")

    command remove:
        name str
        calls fn():
            print("remove {name}")
### ARGS ###
remote
origin
### STDOUT ###
add origin timeout=30

### TITLE ###
NoDefaultStillErrors
### DESCRIPTION ###
The regression guard: without a default, naming no command is still an error.
Pairs with ErrorsIfCommandNotSpecified in cmds.snap.
### INPUT ###
command add:
    *tokens str
    calls fn():
        print("add {tokens}")

command list:
    calls fn():
        print("list")
### ARGS ###
15m
standup
### STDERR ###
Too many positional arguments. Unused: [15m, standup]

Usage:
  TestCase [command] [OPTIONS]

Commands:
  add
  list

Global options:
  -h, --help            Print usage string.
  -i, --interactive     Interactively prompt for script args not already provided, then run.
  -d, --debug           Enables debug output. Intended for Rad script developers.
      --color mode      Control output colorization. Valid values: [auto, always, never] (default auto)
  -q, --quiet           Suppresses some output.
      --confirm-shell   Confirm all shell commands before running them.
      --tls-insecure    Skip TLS certificate verification for all HTTP requests.
      --src             Instead of running the target script, just print it out.
### EXIT ###
1

### TITLE ###
HelpShowsDefaultAndItsEquivalent
### INPUT ###
args:
    repeat r str?   # Repeat interval.

command add:
    ---
    Add a reminder.
    ---
    *tokens str     # Time spec followed by message.
    default
    calls fn():
        print("add")

command list:
    ---
    Show upcoming reminders.
    ---
    calls fn():
        print("list")
### ARGS ###
--help
### STDOUT ###
Usage:
  TestCase [command] [OPTIONS]
  TestCase [tokens...] [OPTIONS]   (same as: TestCase add)

Commands:
  add    Add a reminder. (default)
  list   Show upcoming reminders.

Args for default command 'add':
      --tokens [strs...]   Time spec followed by message.
  -r, --repeat str         (optional) Repeat interval.

Global options:
  -h, --help            Print usage string.
  -i, --interactive     Interactively prompt for script args not already provided, then run.
  -d, --debug           Enables debug output. Intended for Rad script developers.
      --color mode      Control output colorization. Valid values: [auto, always, never] (default auto)
  -q, --quiet           Suppresses some output.
      --confirm-shell   Confirm all shell commands before running them.
      --tls-insecure    Skip TLS certificate verification for all HTTP requests.
      --src             Instead of running the target script, just print it out.

### TITLE ###
BareInvocationWithRequiredDefaultShowsHelp
### DESCRIPTION ###
Routing a bare invocation would answer "missing required argument" and never
mention that other commands exist. Help answers both questions. RAW_ARGS with
nothing in it because --color=never would itself count as an argument.
### INPUT ###
command add:
    tokens str
    default
    calls fn():
        print("add {tokens}")

command list:
    calls fn():
        print("list")
### RAW_ARGS ###
### STDOUT ###
Usage:
  TestCase [command] [OPTIONS]
  TestCase <tokens> [OPTIONS]   (same as: TestCase add)

Commands:
  add    (default)
  list

Args for default command 'add':
      --tokens str
